.TH WAYHINT 1 2026-09-26 "wayhint 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wayhint \- control the wayhint overlay and edit its hint sheets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wayhint
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wayhint
shows the shortcuts, commands and notes you wrote for the window in front of you, in an overlay
drawn by
.BR wayhintd (1).
The hints are YAML files, one per app or terminal command (a
.IR sheet ),
under
.IR ~/.config/wayhint/hints/ .
Nothing in a sheet is ever executed: commands are shown and copied only.
.PP
There are three kinds of command.
The overlay commands send one line to
.B wayhintd
and need it running.
The checking commands read the files themselves and work without the daemon.
The editing commands write sheets directly; the daemon notices the change on its own.
.SH OVERLAY COMMANDS
Each accepts
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
to use another socket than the default.
.TP
.B toggle
Show the overlay for the focused window, or hide it if it is visible.
.TP
.B show
Resolve the context and show the overlay.
.TP
.B hide
Hide the overlay. In search or edit mode the mode and any draft are kept, as with
.BR toggle .
.TP
.B refresh
If the overlay is visible, resolve the focused window again.
.TP
.B reload
Re-read
.I config.yaml
and the sheets.
.TP
.B ping
Check that the daemon is running; prints its pid and the number of sheets.
.TP
.BR context " [" \-\-shown ]
Print the context the daemon resolves right now and the sheet it would pick.
With
.BR \-\-shown ,
print the overlay on screen as it was opened instead, and what narrowed its hints.
Run from a terminal, the plain form sees
.B wayhint
itself as the command in it; use
.B \-\-shown
there.
.TP
.B search\-mode
Enter search mode in the overlay; again to leave, keeping the filter.
Refused while in edit mode.
.TP
.B edit\-mode
Enter or leave edit mode in the overlay.
.SH CHECKING COMMANDS
.TP
.BR validate " [" \-\-config\-dir
.IR DIR ]
Check
.I config.yaml
and every sheet of the configured language.
Warnings are printed but do not fail.
.TP
.BR check\-sheet " [" \-\-strict "] [" \-\-config\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.I PATH
\&...
.br
Check sheet files one by one, installed or not.
Its errors are the ones that keep a sheet from loading.
It also warns about a match pattern that matches every window, a sheet nothing can show,
a hint whose kind and fields disagree, and an include or id that clashes with the installed
sheets.
With
.BR \-\-strict ,
warnings fail too.
.TP
.BI inspect " SHEET" " \fR[\fP\-\-parent" " ID\fR]\fP"
Show what the sheet's includes let through and, given an assumed parent sheet, how many of its
hints are mixed in.
.SH EDITING COMMANDS
Each names the sheet with
.BI \-\-sheet " ID"
and writes nothing while
.B validate
would report anything, warnings included.
.TP
.BI add " TITLE"
Add a hint.
Fields are given with
.BR \-\-kind " {" shortcut , command , tip , note "},"
.BI \-\-key " KEY" \fR,\fP
.BI \-\-command " COMMAND" \fR,\fP
.BI \-\-category " CATEGORY"
and
.BI \-\-remark " TEXT" \fR.\fP
The kind decides which of key and command it takes.
.TP
.BI edit " ID"
Change fields of one hint: the options of
.B add
and
.BI \-\-title " TITLE" \fR.\fP
.TP
.BI remove " ID"
Delete one hint.
.TP
.BI favorite " ID" " \fR[\fP\-\-off\fR]\fP"
Mark a hint as favorite, or clear it with
.BR \-\-off .
.TP
.BI move " ID" " \fR{\fPup\fR|\fPdown\fR}\fP"
Swap a hint with the one above or below it.
.TP
.BR format " [" \-\-modeline "] [" \fIPATH\fP ...]
Rewrite sheets (default: every sheet) in canonical form.
.B \-\-modeline
also adds the yaml-language-server modeline.
.TP
.BR schema " [" \-\-write
.RI [ PATH ]]
Print the JSON Schema for sheets, or write it to
.I PATH
(default:
.B editor.schema_path
in
.IR config.yaml ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help, for
.B wayhint
or for one command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A problem in the files, a refused request, or an error writing.
.TP
.B 2
.B wayhintd
is not running or cannot be reached (overlay commands).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The configuration is read from
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wayhint/
(default
.IR ~/.config/wayhint/ ).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
The daemon's socket is
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wayhint.sock .
Without it,
.IR /tmp/wayhint\- UID /wayhint.sock
is used, only if that directory is the user's own with mode 0700.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
In this order, the first one set picks the language of the interface and of the sheets when
.B language
is
.BR auto .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wayhint/config.yaml
Global settings.
.TP
.IR ~/.config/wayhint/hints/ LANG /*.yaml
Hint sheets. The file name without the extension is the sheet's id.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/wayhint/state.yaml
What the daemon remembers between runs: the search filter of each sheet.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/wayhint/examples/
A configuration and sheets to start from.
.TP
.I /usr/share/wayhint/scripts/setup\-terminals
Points terminal launchers at wrappers that let wayhint tell terminal windows apart.
Writes nothing without
.BR \-\-apply .
.TP
.I /usr/share/wayhint/skills/wayhint\-add\-sheet/
A skill for coding agents that writes a sheet and checks it with
.BR check\-sheet .
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a sheet before putting it in place:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wayhint check\-sheet \-\-strict vi.yaml
.EE
.RE
.PP
Add a hint to the sheet
.BR vi :
.PP
.RS
.EX
wayhint add "Replace in the whole file" \-\-kind command \e
    \-\-command ':%s/old/new/g' \-\-sheet vi
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wayhintd (1)
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/wayhint/
(README.md, SHEET-FORMAT.md, SHEETS.md, CONFIG.md, HOTKEYS.md, TERMINALS.md)
.PP
.UR https://github.com/yasuoeto/wayhint
.UE
